sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant Kafka as Kafka<br/>order.confirmed
  participant Consumer as Kitchen<br/>OrderConfirmedConsumer
  participant Repo as KdsRedisRepository
  participant Redis as Redis<br/>projection keys
  participant Pub as KitchenEventsPublisher

  Kafka->>Consumer: Message value
  Consumer->>Consumer: Parse JSON
  alt Malformed JSON or invalid schema
    Consumer-->>Kafka: Ignore and log warning
  else Valid order.confirmed schema
    Consumer->>Repo: createTicketsFromConfirmedOrder(event)
    Repo->>Redis: Claim event dedupe key
    alt Duplicate eventId
      Redis-->>Repo: Dedupe key exists
      Repo-->>Consumer: No queue events
    else Fresh event
      Repo->>Repo: Partition items by station
      alt Item missing station
        Repo->>Redis: Append dead-letter sample
      else Valid station items
        Repo->>Redis: Claim order+station dedupe key
        Repo->>Redis: Create ticket and item hashes<br/>queue members, SLA, revision
        Repo-->>Consumer: kds.queue_changed events
        Consumer->>Pub: publishMany(events)
      end
    end
  end

  Note over Consumer,Redis: Kitchen accepts only the event contract it understands.<br/>Dedupe is by eventId and by order+station identity.
